            <name>Commercial roof search</name>
            <Placemark id="90441">
                <name>Park Hill School District – Chinn ES, Lakeview MS, Park Hill</name>
                <description>storm damage follow-up → public bid (hail remediation) | Storm 2026-03-10 (KC Northland 3–4.5" hail); bid posted 2026-09-10, mandatory pre-bid 9/16, due 2026-09-30 1:00 PM
Sealed bids for "2026 Roofing Projects – Roof Remediation From Hail Damage" at five schools: shingle replacement, wood deck/blocking replacement, METAL ROOF RECOATING, gutters/downspouts, flashing; complete by Dec 31, 2026; 5% bid bond, prevailing wage. The listing does not name the storm date; the schools sit in the 3/10/2026 Northland hail swath (SPC 4.5" at 1 NE Weatherby Lake), so the link is likely but unconfirmed. Use as a relationship/next-bid target with Facilities.
Contact: Jeremie Kahler, Director of Facilities (named on bid); Support Services · 816-359-4100 (Support Services main line)
Source: https://civiciq.com/public-rfp/park-hill-school-district-2026-roofing-projects-roof-remediation-from-hail-damage</description>
                <styleUrl>#90442</styleUrl>
                <Point id="90440">
                    <coordinates>-94.6886,39.2097,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="90446">
                <name>Former Country Peddler building (roof lost) + City of Garnet</name>
                <description>storm damage to commercial/municipal roofs | Storm 2026-03-10 ~10:30 PM CDT; article 2026-03-23
KOFO: NWS-confirmed downburst up to 85 mph; "The former Country Peddler building lost its roof, the city maintenance shed was blown away and left in the bleachers at the Garnett stadium." County and insurers were still assessing; EM asked anyone with damage claims to notify her office. Building owner of the Country Peddler building not named (not looked up in parcels).
Contact: Sarah Wilper-Burkhart, Director, Anderson County Emergency Management (collecting damage reports) · 785-448-6797 (office) · shulcy@andersoncountyks.org
Source: https://kofo.com/2026/03/23/garnett-storm-damage/</description>
                <styleUrl>#90447</styleUrl>
                <Point id="90445">
                    <coordinates>-95.2419,38.2836,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="90451">
                <name>Kankakee School District 111 – all 12 buildings (Kankakee HS</name>
                <description>storm damage to commercial/municipal roofs | Storm 2026-03-10; articles 2026-03-15, 2026-03-26, 2026-05-01
Hail (record 6"+ stones) and EF-3 tornado: "thousands and thousands of holes" in the KHS roof; insurers called 9 of 12 roofs a total loss; by May 1 damage estimated $28.7M, roof damage to all 12 buildings (10 must be replaced) ≈ $21M; repairs over 2–3 years; priorities KHS, Aroma Park bldg, Kennedy MS, Kankakee JHS; several million in rooftop HVAC too; older (20+ yr) roofs covered at actual cash value.
Contact: District central office (Asst. Supt. of Business Services quoted: Lyle/Harrison Neal; Supt. Dr. Teresa Lance) · 815-802-7730 (district main)
Source: https://www.shawlocal.com/daily-journal/2026/04/30/storm-damage-nears-30m-for-kankakee-school-district/ ; https://www.shawlocal.com/daily-journal/2026/03/26/kankakee-schools-assessing-storm-damage/</description>
                <styleUrl>#90452</styleUrl>
                <Point id="90450">
                    <coordinates>-87.8804,41.1003,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="90456">
                <name>Bishop McNamara Catholic School – Kankakee site (550 W Brook</name>
                <description>storm damage to commercial/institutional roofs | Storm 2026-03-10; article 2026-03-15
"The Kankakee site took extensive damage, including 30 broken skylights, broken windows and roof and water damage." School said "the replacement to the roof, windows, floor, buses, HVAC and exterior facilities will take time." Servpro and PSI Construction did initial assessment.
Contact: School office (Kankakee site) · (815) 932-7413
Source: https://www.shawlocal.com/daily-journal/2026/03/15/school-resuming-this-week-after-storms/</description>
                <styleUrl>#90457</styleUrl>
                <Point id="90455">
                    <coordinates>-87.877,41.0964,0.0</coordinates>
                </Point>
            </Placemark>
            <Placemark id="90461">
                <name>Kankakee Community College – Riverfront Campus + manufacturi</name>
                <description>storm damage to commercial/institutional roofs | Storm 2026-03-10; article 2026-03-15
KCC closed its Riverfront Campus and local manufacturing extensions while crews assessed storm damage and began repairs; reopened Mar 16. Roof damage not itemized in the article.
Contact: No contact found
Source: https://www.shawlocal.com/daily-journal/2026/03/15/school-resuming-this-week-after-storms/</description>
